:"2026-08-25","reportDate":"2026-08-25","cik":"0001810997","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810997/000119312526364050/d75446dex992.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8c9750cde037514161c3f0681fffb0cd049ba29ae420550994bd12a69c10c7f1.bin","sha256":"8c9750cde037514161c3f0681fffb0cd049ba29ae420550994bd12a69c10c7f1"}},{"id":"e728a5c99590e6e3c7784c09fcabeb894410665137d029ca2efd5725e63efa06","quote":"As of June 30, 2026, the Group obtained secured borrowings from several banks of RMB9.64 billion in aggregate. The maturity dates ranged from July 2026 to June 2035. As of December 31, 2025, the Group obtained secured borrowings from several banks of RMB8.16 billion in aggregate. The maturity dates ranged from January 2026 to June 2035.","context":"6","section":"MANAGEMENT DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS","block":99,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-364050","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-25","reportDate":"2026-08-25","cik":"0001810997","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810997/000119312526364050/d75446dex992.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8c9750cde037514161c3f0681fffb0cd049ba29ae420550994bd12a69c10c7f1.bin","sha256":"8c9750cde037514161c3f0681fffb0cd049ba29ae420550994bd12a69c10c7f1"}},{"id":"2d465e0eceaaac9ead5c4d003a732035cc4a29bfc80a5ddda914ea9a6b018a12","quote":"Moreover, the Group received subsidies from the local government for interest expenses incurred associated with the borrowings. As of June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025, the aggregate sum of loans receiving government-subsidized interest amounted to RMB2.94 billion and RMB3.48 billion, respectively. For the six months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, the Group recognized the subsidies to reduce the related interest expenses as incurred or to reduce the interest expenses capitalized in the construction costs of certain manufacturing plant or base, if any.","context":"As of June 30, 2026, the Group obtained secured borrowings from several banks of RMB9.64 billion in aggregate. The maturity dates ranged from July 2026 to June 2035. As of December 31, 2025, the Group obtained secured borrowings from several banks of RMB8.16 billion in aggregate. The maturity dates ranged from January 2026 to June 2035.","section":"MANAGEMENT DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS","block":100,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-364050","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-25","reportDate":"2026-08-25","cik":"0001810997","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810997/000119312526364050/d75446dex992.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8c9750cde037514161c3f0681fffb0cd049ba29ae420550994bd12a69c10c7f1.bin","sha256":"8c9750cde037514161c3f0681fffb0cd049ba29ae420550994bd12a69c10c7f1"}},{"id":"d948cdeec9d9b2aaff0c5b050bbd09884bf6d4c06ffef7a7f962cb936b3b22f7","quote":"In March 2024 and October 2024, the Group entered into asset-backed securitization arrangements with third-party financial institutions and set up two securitization vehicles to issue senior debt securities to third party investors, which are collateralized by installment payment receivables (the “ABS transferred financial assets”). The Group also acts as a servicer to provide management, administration and collection services on the ABS transferred financial assets and has the power to direct the activities that most significantly impact the securitization vehicles. The economic interests are retained by the Group in the form of subordinated interests as well as its obligation to absorb losses under certain circumstances. As a result, the Group consolidated the securitization vehicles. The proceeds from the issuance of debt securities are reported as securitization debt. The securities will be repaid as collections on the underlying collateralized assets occur and the amounts were included in “Long-term borrowings, current portion” or “Long-term borrowings” according to the contractual maturities of the debt securities. As of June 30, 2026, the balance of current and non-current portion of the ABS were RMB0.05 billion and nil, respectively. As of December 31, 2025, the balance of current and non-current portion of the ABS were RMB0.27 billion and RMB0.002 billion, respectively.","context":"Asset-backed securities (“ABS”)","section":"MANAGEMENT DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS","block":103,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-364050","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-25","reportDate":"2026-08-25","cik":"0001810997","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810997/000119312526364050/d75446dex992.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8c9750cde037514161c3f0681fffb0cd049ba29ae420550994bd12a69c10c7f1.bin","sha256":"8c9750cde037514161c3f0681fffb0cd049ba29ae420550994bd12a69c10c7f1"}},{"id":"ab5264ce7ecc530a466f259bbcfb0fae3b1d4deeb6f0fd0045f4a63f35139cf9","quote":"As of June 30, 2026, all of the bank loans and other borrowings of the Group were denominated in RMB and bore fixed and floating interest rates, and the Group had not been in violation of any of the covenants pursuant to the applicable agreement(s) entered with the lenders.","context":"ities to third party investors, which are collateralized by installment payment receivables (the “ABS transferred financial assets”). The Group also acts as a servicer to provide management, administration and collection services on the ABS transferred financial assets and has the power to direct the activities that most significantly impact the securitization vehicles. The economic interests are retained by the Group in the form of subordinated interests as well as its obligation to absorb losses under certain circumstances. As a result, the Group consolidated the securitization vehicles. The proceeds from the issuance of debt securities are reported as securitization debt. The securities will be repaid as collections on the underlying collateralized assets occur and the amounts were included in “Long-term borrowings, current portion” or “Long-term borrowings” according to the contractual maturities of the debt securities. As of June 30, 2026, the balance of current and non-current portion of the ABS were RMB0.05 billion and nil, respectively. As of December 31, 2025, the balance of current and non-current portion of the ABS were RMB0.27 billion and RMB0.002 billion, respectively.","section":"MANAGEMENT DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS","block":104,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-364050","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-25","reportDate":"2026-08-25","cik":"0001810997","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810997/000119312526364050/d75446dex992.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8c9750cde037514161c3f0681fffb0cd049ba29ae420550994bd12a69c10c7f1.bin","sha256":"8c9750cde037514161c3f0681fffb0cd049ba29ae420550994bd12a69c10c7f1"}},{"id":"c8ee8a92c14841c1f9eba89cdfc4a888cad3854d853a3ab0f70e449ffa1101ed","quote":"As of June 30, 2026, the Group pledged restricted cash and restricted deposits of RMB9.62 billion (December 31, 2025: RMB8.44 billion) for bank borrowings and the issuance of letter of guarantee, bank notes, legal disputes and others. Certain manufacturing buildings of Guangzhou plants, Wuhan base and Zhaoqing plants, the land use right of Wuhan base, Guangzhou plants, and Guangzhou Xiaopeng technology park and the equipments of Wuhan base were secured for the long-term bank loan with a total appraised value of RMB6.60 billion (December 31, 2025: RMB5.80 billion).","context":"Pledge of assets","section":"MANAGEMENT DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS","block":107,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-364050","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-08-25","reportDate":"2026-08-25","cik":"0001810997","url"